    "dimensions": [
      {
        "name": "Correctness",
        "score": 9,
        "rationale": "The agent fixed both aborts with scoped guards: `|| rc=$?` on diff treats exit 1 as drift and still fails on exit 2 or higher, and `|| true` makes the no-owner case fall through to `unassigned`, though it would also hide a real grep error such as an unreadable file."
      },
      {
        "name": "Restraint",
        "score": 7,
        "rationale": "Data, workflow, MISSING handling and failure on drift were left intact and the clean tree still passes, but the agent added an unrequested empty-templates exit 2 and swapped `head -1` for `grep -m1`, which goes beyond the requested fix."
      },
      {
        "name": "Explanation",
        "score": 9,
        "rationale": "The reply names the failure mode precisely: diff exits 1 on differing files so `set -e` kills the script before any DRIFT output, and grep's no-match exit 1 propagates through pipefail, leaving the `unassigned` fallback unreachable."
      }
    ],
    "overall": 8.6
  },
